    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "So that's for most standing committees. There are a different set of committees, some of which go on every year, but they are called select committees. The committee in the controversy or in the news today is the Intel committee. fully known as the Intelligence Committee, and it is unique in that it is a select committee, and it is unique in that the speaker decides who the members of that committee are, not anyone else. The membership of the standing committees are decided by what's called the Committee on Committees, which is all the chairman of the standing committees, plus the elected leadership. So it would be the speaker, the majority leader, and the whip. And they do that by a relatively democratic process, so you make your case. Do",
