    "turn_text": "i would argue that adam shift absolutely was the person who changed the tradition he broke the tradition the tradition was something that was imbued upon members who got to serve on Intel, which they did by expertise, knowledge in the area, interest shown in the area, but also by honoring the tradition. So, for example, you were told that the information that you were given in the Intel Committee was to be kept within the Intel Committee and not discussed amongst other members of Congress because it was classified information. One of my best friends, and for a part of the time that I was there, my best friend, was at Pete Hookstra of Michigan. He became the chair, who became the chair of the Intel Committee. And there were countless times when I would talk to Pete about issues and ask him something that went to an Intel issue and he'd say, John, I'd love to tell you, but I can't tell you. And Adam Schiff blew that tradition badly and then history proved him not to have been truthful in doing that. I mean you can get away if what you're talking about is a secret that nobody knows, as Mr. McCarthy just described, you can get away with lying about it and in this case years go by before anybody figures out that, wait a minute, Adam Schiff lied when he said this or that or the other thing. In part, what is happening here is Adam Schiff, I would argue, disqualified himself. He",
